$ kyp 
[stderr]
kyp 0.1.0: Keep Your Prompts from the command line.

Usage: kyp <command> [arguments] [flags]

Prompts in your app (delivery key: KYP_DELIVERY_KEY):
  pull       Write the deployed prompts of an app environment to a snapshot (uses KYP_DELIVERY_KEY).
  get        Print a deployed prompt, rendered, from a snapshot folder or the delivery mirrors.

Your workspace (API key: kyp login or KYP_API_KEY):
  login      Store a workspace API key (kyp_live_…) in the OS config folder, readable only by you.
  logout     Remove the stored API key.
  search     Search prompts (full text and semantic).
  ls         List the prompts in your workspace.
  show       Print a prompt's body (details go to stderr).
  push       Create a prompt from FILE (- for stdin), or save it as a new version of an existing one.
  diff       Word diff between two versions of a prompt (red: removed, green: added).
  deploy     Deploy prompt versions to an app environment (a new revision; apps pick it up within seconds).
  rollback   Roll an app environment back to an earlier revision (published as a new revision).
  capture    Send text from stdin to the workspace Inbox, to promote into a prompt later.

Other:
  mcp        Print MCP server config for Claude Code, Cursor and VS Code.
  version    Print the kyp version.

Every command takes --json (machine-readable output) and --color=auto|always|never.
Run "kyp help <command>" for its flags. Exit codes: 0 ok, 1 error, 2 usage, 3 auth,
4 not found, 5 conflict, 6 unavailable, 7 invalid input, 8 quota.
[exit 2]

