$ kyp help deploy
Usage: kyp deploy APP ENV NAME=SLUG[@VERSION]... [-m MESSAGE]

Deploy prompt versions to an app environment (a new revision; apps pick it up within seconds).

Flags:
  --api-url string       API base URL (default $KYP_API_URL or https://api.keepyourprompts.com)
  --color string         colour output: auto, always or never (default auto)
  --json                 print JSON
  -m string              same as --message
  --message string       deploy message
[exit 0]

$ kyp push --help
Usage: kyp push FILE --name NAME [--slug SLUG] [-m MESSAGE] [--base N]

Create a prompt from FILE (- for stdin), or save it as a new version of an existing one.

Flags:
  --api-url string       API base URL (default $KYP_API_URL or https://api.keepyourprompts.com)
  --base int             the version your edit started from (default: the current version); an older one fails with a conflict
  --color string         colour output: auto, always or never (default auto)
  --json                 print JSON
  --kind string          kind when creating: prompt, system_prompt, skill, agent, mcp_config, snippet or test_set (default prompt)
  -m string              same as --message
  --message string       version message
  --name string          display name (required to create; default slug derives from it)
  --slug string          prompt slug, e.g. support/triage (default: from --name)
[exit 0]

